   "text": "Chapter 8. Data Types"
  },
  {
   "kind": "early",
   "text": "PostgreSQL has a rich set of native data types available to users",
   "where": "p < div#DATATYPE.chapter < div#docContent < div#pgContentWrap.col-11 < div.row"
  },
  {
   "kind": "mid",
   "text": "The following types (or spellings thereof) are specified by SQL: bigint, bit",
   "where": "p < div.note < div#DATATYPE.chapter < div#docContent < div#pgContentWrap.col-11"
  },
  {
   "kind": "late",
   "text": "Each data type has an external representation determined by its input and",
   "where": "p < div#DATATYPE.chapter < div#docContent < div#pgContentWrap.col-11 < div.row"
  },
  {
   "kind": "table_row",
   "text": "real float4 single precision floating-point number (4 bytes)",
